---
description: Safety rules for content scripts, third-party DOM adapters, and destructive site operations.
globs: ["apps/**/entrypoints/content*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}", "apps/**/lib/adapters/**/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}"]
alwaysApply: false
---

Third-party websites are unstable and untrusted integration surfaces.

- Keep selectors, parsers, compatibility probes, and site operations inside the site adapter.
- Validate expected page/API shape before acting.
- Fail closed when compatibility checks fail; never guess a destructive selector.
- Do not scatter host class names or selectors through UI/domain code.
- For delete/archive/send/submit/bulk-edit actions, require explicit user intent, accurate target scope, bounded concurrency, and per-item result reporting.
- Do not implement hidden retries that could duplicate a side effect.
- Undocumented/private web APIs must be documented as fragile in the app SPEC and tested behind an adapter.
